{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794128492,"nonce":"UOprbDsfVCef4herGcTEkkXcLkw=","message":"Reproduced on the Ubuntu NUC with a headless cn input (Hybrid theme, 43 characters): the caret and the drawn text end disagree. A second defect hid behind the first: the widgets measured with the registry's default font, not the family the field is drawn in. On the NUC the default is Ubuntu and the field draws in Noto Sans, so the two errors nearly cancelled (caret 288.75, text end 287) and fixing only the spacing would have moved the caret 13px left of the text. The fix measures with one TextFace taken from the field's own rules (family, weight, style, letter spacing): caret, selection, wrap, hit-test and scroll in text_input and text_area. Tests: unit tests per widget (red before), and recorder test cn_input_caret, red on the NUC at origin/main and green with the fix, green on macOS. Limit: values inherited from an ancestor are not read, same as the field's font size today; the rules on the field itself are. Working tree, not yet committed.","files":null}]}